_Lines and Surfaces_ is a `Java` application that lets you view parametrized surfaces and curves in three dimensions.

These are *surfaces* given by a function $\mathbf{f}$:
$$ \mathbf{f}:(u,v)\in \mathbb{R^2} \rightarrow (f_1(u,v), f_2(u,v), f_3(u,v))^{T}$$
These are *curves* given by a function $\boldsymbol{\gamma}$:

$$\boldsymbol{\gamma}:t\in\mathbb{R}\rightarrow(\gamma_1(t), \gamma_2(t), \gamma_3(t))^{T}$$

The `UI` accepts the usual syntax for defining functions. It supports the operators `+, -, *, /, ^` and functions such as `sin, cos, exp, tan, ln, ...`. After setting up your _curve_ or _surface_, you can generate a `.obj` file by pressing the `g` key.

Feel free to download the program below.

![*Lines and Surfaces* app video](https://youtu.be/PRomaGN4ENg)

